{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":46.5,"text":"In 1889, Paris was preparing an enormous party, the World Fair, and the engineer Gustave Eiffel promised it a gateway that would be the tallest tower on earth. His team joined about 18,000 pieces of iron with two and a half million rivets, and in a little over two years, the tower reached 300 meters. Many Parisians thought it hideous and asked for it to be pulled down. That was not unreasonable. The permit said it would stand for 20 years and then be sold for scrap. What saved it was something nobody had imagined while it was being designed. It was the tallest thing in the city, which made it the perfect place for aerials, and once radio mattered, the tower became useful. It was not saved because people grew to love it. It was saved because it was needed.","words":[{"word":"In","start":0,"end":0.41999998688697815},{"word":"1889","start":0.41999998688697815,"end":1.4199999570846558},{"word":"Paris","start":1.8799999952316284,"end":1.9800000190734863},{"word":"was","start":1.9800000190734863,"end":2.319999933242798},{"word":"preparing","start":2.319999933242798,"end":2.5799999237060547},{"word":"an","start":2.5799999237060547,"end":3.059999942779541},{"word":"enormous","start":3.059999942779541,"end":3.5},{"word":"party","start":3.5,"end":3.859999895095825},{"word":"the","start":4.28000020980835,"end":4.440000057220459},{"word":"World","start":4.440000057220459,"end":4.71999979019165},{"word":"Fair","start":4.71999979019165,"end":4.960000038146973},{"word":"and","start":5.420000076293945,"end":5.619999885559082},{"word":"the","start":5.619999885559082,"end":6.300000190734863},{"word":"engineer","start":6.300000190734863,"end":6.300000190734863},{"word":"Gustave","start":6.300000190734863,"end":6.78000020980835},{"word":"Eiffel","start":6.78000020980835,"end":7.21999979019165},{"word":"promised","start":7.21999979019165,"end":7.820000171661377},{"word":"it","start":7.820000171661377,"end":8.0600004196167